WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:02.223
- We won in the Revolution.

00:00:02.223 --> 00:00:04.350
- We won in everything.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.509
- America.

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:09.665
(classical piano and cello music)

00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:26.181
- Maltesers.

00:00:26.181 --> 00:00:27.978
Isn't that a dog? A Maltese?

00:00:27.978 --> 00:00:30.439
- It kinda tastes like a more
chocolatey Kit Kat to me.

00:00:30.439 --> 00:00:34.234
- If Whoppers had more chocolate
around it, that is that.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.486
- How the chocolate's
like unusually smooth.

00:00:36.486 --> 00:00:38.822
- You could sneak this into
the movies, like really easily.

00:00:38.822 --> 00:00:40.207
- Ooh, this is good movie candy.

00:00:40.207 --> 00:00:41.401
Like you could put it with your popcorn?

00:00:41.401 --> 00:00:43.642
- Nice packaging, though.
- Yeah. It's cute.

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:45.076
- Can just, like, hide it in a purse.

00:00:45.076 --> 00:00:46.666
- Like if it was the
only thing in the house

00:00:46.666 --> 00:00:48.569
I would still eat it.

00:00:48.569 --> 00:00:50.375
- Why would they call it Dairy Milk?

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:51.960
It's a chocolate bar.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.213
- Isn't all milk dairy?

00:00:53.213 --> 00:00:55.018
- Dairy Milk sounds like a yogurt brand,

00:00:55.018 --> 00:00:57.340
or like, if I was gonna
buy, like ricotta cheese.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:00.343
- This reminds me of the
Willy Wonka wrapping.

00:01:00.343 --> 00:01:02.053
- I was kind of expecting
something to be in the

00:01:02.053 --> 00:01:03.889
middle, 'cause they look like pockets.

00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:05.140
- This is solid.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.933
Like, you could build
something with these.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.286
- You know how there's,
like, Double Stuf Oreos,

00:01:08.286 --> 00:01:09.677
it's like a Double Stuf Hershey's.

00:01:09.677 --> 00:01:12.231
I would prefer a Hershey's bar over this.

00:01:12.231 --> 00:01:13.395
- [Voiceover] Yorkie.

00:01:13.395 --> 00:01:16.485
- [Voiceover] Isn't there a
candy already titled Yorkies?

00:01:16.485 --> 00:01:19.488
- Dogs are cute. Maybe--
- Hope the chocolate's cute.

00:01:19.488 --> 00:01:21.239
- Haha, looks like a Lego.

00:01:21.239 --> 00:01:22.449
(chocolate snaps)
- Ooh!

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.826
(laughs)
It's very dense.

00:01:24.826 --> 00:01:26.787
- It's like the chocolate on Nestle Crunch

00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:28.268
but without the crunch.

00:01:28.268 --> 00:01:29.706
- A weak Ghirardelli.

00:01:29.706 --> 00:01:32.178
- Nothing special. Pretty generic.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.253
- [Voiceover] Flake. New peel and reveal.

00:01:35.253 --> 00:01:37.506
- Cover Girl, like, "New peel and reveal!"

00:01:37.506 --> 00:01:38.382
Like, something like that.

00:01:38.382 --> 00:01:39.886
- It sounds like a face mask.

00:01:39.886 --> 00:01:42.453
- This looks very interesting.

00:01:42.453 --> 00:01:44.796
- It's like bark. It looks like trees. Oh.

00:01:44.796 --> 00:01:45.699
(giggles)

00:01:46.683 --> 00:01:47.723
- It has a weird texture.

00:01:47.723 --> 00:01:49.142
- It confuses me.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.603
- It definitely lives up to the name.

00:01:51.603 --> 00:01:53.230
- Yeah.
- It's very flaky.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:55.774
- It kind of tastes like the powder

00:01:55.774 --> 00:01:58.026
you make with hot chocolate?

00:01:58.026 --> 00:02:00.374
- There's, like, a buttery taste to it.

00:02:00.374 --> 00:02:04.115
- It tastes very good! I'm impressed.

00:02:04.115 --> 00:02:05.570
- [Voiceover] Toffee Crisp.

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:08.245
- [Voiceover] It looked like
Reese's when I first saw it.

00:02:08.245 --> 00:02:09.830
- I don't know what toffee is.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.382
- Oh. Oh, wow.
- All right.

00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:15.544
- Oh, I like this. It
has so much happening.

00:02:15.544 --> 00:02:19.154
- Say, like a combination
of a Kit Kat and a Twix?

00:02:19.154 --> 00:02:22.454
- Crispy, chewy. True.

00:02:22.454 --> 00:02:23.902
- Wow.
- Mmm, this is good.

00:02:23.902 --> 00:02:26.170
- It's kinda like a
crunch bar on the bottom.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:26.988
- Wow.

00:02:26.988 --> 00:02:28.943
- I don't know what's
in the middle of this.

00:02:28.943 --> 00:02:30.181
Something crunchy.

00:02:30.181 --> 00:02:31.761
- It's toffee! That's what toffee is.

00:02:31.761 --> 00:02:34.104
- That's what, oh, then, I
guess that's what toffee is.

00:02:34.104 --> 00:02:35.128
- Wow!

00:02:35.128 --> 00:02:37.315
- Why don't they just change the wrapper?

00:02:37.315 --> 00:02:38.733
That just seems easy.

00:02:38.733 --> 00:02:41.611
- I'm almost borderlining
on emotionally unstable if

00:02:41.611 --> 00:02:43.446
these aren't going to
be in America anymore.

00:02:43.446 --> 00:02:45.483
'Cause we're really just
starting out a new relationship

00:02:45.483 --> 00:02:49.057
here, and I'm feeling
like it's really positive.

00:02:49.057 --> 00:02:53.693
(classical piano and cello music)

00:02:54.044 --> 00:02:56.274
(swishing and old, creaky sign swinging)

